letes/59779"} "Ion Draica"] ". Korban was the 1979 World and 1980 European Champion, while Draica had won the 1978 Worlds and was European Champion from 1977-79. In the first two rounds, however, Draica lost both matches when he was disqualified for passivity, which eliminated him from the tournament. After four rounds Korban and Bulgarian " [:a {:href "/athletes/57449"} "Pavel Pavlov"] ", bronze medalist at the 1979 Worlds and 1980 Europeans, were tied with only 1.0 bad points, and advanced to the final round along with Poland’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/59625"} "Jan Dołgowicz"] ", runner-up at the 1978-79 Europeans. Korban had already defeated Dołgowicz by decision in round four, so when he defeated Pavlov in the first round of the final, winning by a 13-7, the gold medal was Korban’s. Pavlov easily threw Dołgowicz in 1:28 to secure the silver medal."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Round Eliminated"] [:th {} "Bad Points"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "250"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/60491"} "Gennady Korban"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/URS.png"}] "URS"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "156"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/59625"} "Jan Dołgowicz"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/POL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/POL.png"}] "POL"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "31"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/57449"} "Pavel Pavlov"]] [:td {} [:a {: